774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[6,9]},{"id":"athaliah_359","name":"Athaliah","also":"","summary":"The daughter of Ahab and Jezebel, and the wife of Jehoram, king of Judah (2 Kings 8:18), who “walked in the ways of the house of Ahab” (2 Chr. 21:6), called “daughter” of Omri (2 Kings 8:26).","verses":15,"father":"Ahab","mother":"Jezebel","v":[7]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[16,25]},{"id":"holy_spirit_7400","name":"Holy Spirit","also":"Comforter, Holy Ghost","summary":"The third Person of the adorable Trinity.","verses":246,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"zacharias_3011","name":"Zacharias","also":"Zechariah","summary":"The son or grandson of Jehoiada, the high priest in the times of Ahaziah and Joash. After the death of Jehoiada he boldly condemned both the king and the people for their rebellion against God (2 Chr. 24:20), which so stirred up their resentment against him that at the king’s commandment they stoned him with stones, and he died “in the court of the house of the Lord” (24:21).","verses":3,"father":"Jehoiada","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"jehozabad_812","name":"Jehozabad","also":"","summary":"The son of Shomer, one of the two conspirators who put king Jehoash to death in Millo in Jerusalem (2 Kings 12:21).","verses":2,"father":"Shimrith","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"shimeath_2683","name":"Shimeath","also":"","summary":"","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"shimrith_2724","name":"Shimrith","also":"Shomer","summary":"The mother of Jehozabad, who murdered Joash (2 Kings 12:21); called also Shimrith, a Moabitess (2 Chr. 24:26).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"zabad_1746","name":"Zabad","also":"Jozachar","summary":"The son of Shemath. He conspired against Joash, king of Judah, and slew him (2 Chr. 24:25, 26).","verses":2,"father":"Shimeath","mother":"","v":[26]},{"id":"amaziah_214","name":"Amaziah","also":"","summary":"The son and successor of Joash, and eighth king of the separate kingdom of Judah (2 Kings 14:1-4). He began his reign by punishing the murderers of his father (5-7; 2 Chr. 25:3-5).","verses":34,"father":"Joash","mother":"Jehoaddan","v":[27]}],"places":[{"id":"beersheba_170","name":"Beersheba","kind":"City","lat":31.245,"lon":34.84068,"summary":"Well of the oath, or well of seven, a well dug by Abraham, and so named because he and Abimelech here entered into a compact (Gen. 21:31). On re-opening it, Isaac gave it the same name (Gen. 26:31-33).","verses":32,"v":[1]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,6,9,18,23]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[23]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3101,7651,7651,1121,1121,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,3389,3389,705,8141,517,517,8034,6645,6645,884,884,884,884],[3101,3101,6213,3477,3477,3477,5869,5869,5869,3068,3068,3068,3605,3117,3117,3077,3077,3548,3548],[3077,5375,0,0,8147,802,3205,3205,3205,1121,1323,1323],[1961,1961,1961,3101,1961,3820,3820,2318,2318,1004,1004,3068,3068,3068],[6908,6908,6908,3548,3548,3881,3881,559,559,3318,3318,5892,5892,5892,3063,3063,6908,6908,3701,3701,1767,8141,3605,3605,3478,2388,2388,1004,1004,430,430,430,1697,1697,4116,3881,3881,3881,3808,3808,4116,4116],[4428,4428,4428,7121,3077,7218,7218,559,559,559,4069,3808,3808,3808,1875,3881,3881,935,935,3063,3063,3389,3389